{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Evaluation</h1>
<p class="lede">Each run below is one directory of <code>evals/reports</code>. Tables show every system and corpus in it,
formatted exactly as the runner wrote them (4 decimals; latency in whole milliseconds).</p>

{{ m.unreadable(data.unreadable['evaluation']) }}

{% if data.groups %}
<nav aria-label="Runs on this page" class="toc">
  <ul>
  {% for g in data.groups %}<li><a href="#{{ g.anchor }}">{{ g.label }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
    <li><a href="#methodology">Methodology</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>
{% for g in data.groups %}
<section aria-labelledby="{{ g.anchor }}">
  <h2 id="{{ g.anchor }}">{{ g.label }}</h2>
  <p class="meta">Reports: <code>{{ g.path }}</code> · code <code>{{ g.git_sha[:12] }}</code>
  {% if g.kind == 'claude' %} · total cost ${{ '%.6f'|format(g.total_cost_usd) }}{% endif %}</p>
  <p class="meta">LLM: <code class="wrap-any">{{ g.llm }}</code></p>
  {% if g.kind == 'offline' %}
  <p class="note">The offline gate uses the in-repo extractive responder, not a language model, on the gate snapshot
  database with no reranker. It measures retrieval, the as-of filter and citation handling. Pull requests are compared
  against these numbers by <code>eval.yml</code>.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {{ m.metrics_table(g, g.label ~ ': every metric') }}

  {% if eval_charts[g.path] %}
  <div class="charts">
    {{ m.legend(g.systems) }}
    {% for svg in eval_charts[g.path] %}<figure class="chart-fig">{{ svg|safe }}</figure>{% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h3 id="{{ g.anchor }}-traps">Trap questions</h3>
  <p>A trap is a question whose answer changed in the next version, so an unfiltered retriever is likely to find the
  newer, wrong text. Trap precision and trap outdated rate are the runner's metrics; the case counts are joined from
  the golden sets' <code>trap</code> flags.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="{{ g.label }} trap breakdown">
  <table>
    <caption>{{ g.label }}: trap vs other cases</caption>
    <thead><tr>
      <th scope="col">Corpus</th><th scope="col">System</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Trap cases</th><th scope="col" class="num">Trap precision</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Trap outdated rate</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Trap cases with an outdated citation</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Other cases</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Other cases with an outdated citation</th>
      <th scope="col" class="num">Declined (trap / other)</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for t in trap_rows[g.path] %}
      <tr{% if t.system == 'driftline' %} class="ours"{% endif %}>
        <th scope="row">{{ t.corpus }}</th><td><code>{{ t.system }}</code></td>
        <td class="num">{{ t.trap_cases }}</td><td class="num">{{ t.trap_precision }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ t.trap_outdated }}</td><td class="num">{{ t.trap_with_outdated }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ t.other_cases }}</td><td class="num">{{ t.other_with_outdated }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ t.trap_declined }} / {{ t.other_declined }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
  {{ m.empty('Evaluation results not yet published', 'No eval report is committed under evals/reports yet.') }}
{% endif %}

<section aria-labelledby="methodology">
  <h2 id="methodology">Methodology</h2>
  <h3>Golden sets</h3>
  <p>The golden questions in <a href="{{ REPO_URL }}/tree/main/evals/golden">evals/golden</a> were drafted by
  <code>claude-haiku-5-5</code> from the real ingested corpora (openFDA/DailyMed drug labels and
  <code>kubernetes/website</code> release branches). Code, not the model, ties each case to a real version id and a
  quote taken from that version's chunks; every kept case passed mechanical validation against the database (the
  version exists, the date lies in its window, the quote is in it, and for a trap the quote is gone from the next
  version). No case was written or edited by hand. Construction details and counts are in
  <a href="{{ REPO_URL }}/blob/main/evals/golden/README.md">evals/golden/README.md</a>.</p>
  {% if h %}
  <h3>Sample versus full set</h3>
  <p>The real-Claude runs used a deterministic stratified sample (one case per kind/trap stratum, the rest shared in
  proportion, cases taken in sha256(id) order), not the full sets:</p>
  <ul>
  {% for c in h.group.corpora %}{% set s = h.strata[c] %}
    <li><strong>{{ c }}</strong>: {{ h.sample_sizes[c] }}{% if c in h.full_set_sizes %} of {{ h.full_set_sizes[c] }}{% endif %} cases:
    {{ s.traps }} traps, {{ s.stable_point_in_time }} stable <code>point_in_time</code>, {{ s.current }} <code>current</code>{% if s.other %}, {{ s.other }} other{% endif %}{% if h.subset_file[c] %};
    the same subset the CI gate uses (<code>evals/snapshot/{{ c }}.jsonl</code>){% endif %}.</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
  <h3>Metric definitions</h3>
  <dl class="defs">
    <dt>Citation precision</dt><dd>Citations whose version was in force at the question's <code>as_of</code> date <em>and</em> whose quote is supported by the cited chunk, divided by all citations, pooled over cases. Partial overlap with an expected version does not count.</dd>
    <dt>Outdated-citation rate</dt><dd>Citations of a real version that was not in force at <code>as_of</code>, divided by all citations.</dd>
    <dt>Trap precision / trap outdated rate</dt><dd>The same two metrics over trap cases only.</dd>
    <dt>Faithfulness (verifier)</dt><dd>Presented claims that pass the verifier's deterministic quote check, divided by all claims.</dd>
    <dt>Insufficient-evidence accuracy</dt><dd>Cases answered when an answer is expected, or declined when the case expects insufficient evidence, divided by all cases.</dd>
    <dt>p95 latency, cost per answer</dt><dd>Per-case wall time and the summed <code>llm_calls.cost_usd</code> of the case.</dd>
    <dt>Stale and error cases</dt><dd>A case whose expected version no longer exists is <code>stale_case</code>: excluded and counted, never scored as a model failure. An error is a system failure.</dd>
  </dl>
  <h3>Systems</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><code>driftline</code></strong>: plan, sub-question fan-out, as-of-filtered hybrid retrieval and rerank, draft, citation verification with up to 2 re-retrievals. Semantic cache off.</li>
    <li><strong><code>plain_rag</code></strong>: the same retriever and reranker with the as-of filter disabled, then one draft with the same model tier and schema. No planner, verifier or re-retrieval; its prompt makes no in-force claim.</li>
    <li><strong><code>no_retrieval</code></strong>: the model alone{% if h and 'no_retrieval' in h.group.missing_systems %} (no report committed yet){% endif %}.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Offline gate versus real Claude</h3>
  <p>The real-Claude runs measure the full product with a language model. The offline gate runs on every pull request
  for free and deterministically, with an extractive responder that cites the first sentence of the top chunks, so
  plain RAG's unfiltered retrieval shows up directly as outdated citations. Its numbers are a regression baseline,
  not a model-quality claim: do not compare the two runs' numbers with each other.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
